    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39340" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Psōphis</span></b> , ī^dis,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ψωφίς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in
			Arcadia</i>, <i>west of the chain of Erymanthus</i>,
			now <i>Tripotamo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 6, 10, § 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
				607</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4, 296</span></i>.— Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Psōphidĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Psophis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 46,
				47, § 151</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 7,
				1, 2</span></i>.</div>
